Customer Shopping Behavior Analysis
Project Overview

This project analyzes customer shopping behavior using SQL, Python, and Power BI. The objective is to uncover purchasing patterns, customer preferences, revenue drivers, and business insights that can help improve decision-making in retail and e-commerce environments.

The project follows a complete analytics workflow:

Data Cleaning
Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA)
Business Analytics using SQL
Interactive Dashboard Development using Power BI
Dataset Description

The dataset contains customer purchase information, demographic details, shopping preferences, and transaction-related attributes.

Features
Column	Description
customer_id	Unique customer identifier
age	Customer age
gender	Customer gender
item_purchased	Product purchased
category	Product category
purchase_amount	Purchase amount
location	Customer location
size	Product size
color	Product color
season	Season of purchase
review_rating	Customer review rating
subscription_status	Subscription membership status
shipping_type	Shipping method selected
discount_applied	Discount usage indicator
previous_purchases	Number of previous purchases
payment_method	Payment method used
frequency_of_purchases	Purchase frequency category
age_group	Customer age segment
purchase_frequency_days	Days between purchases
Project Objectives
Analyze customer purchasing behavior.
Identify top-performing product categories.
Evaluate customer spending patterns.
Study the impact of discounts and subscriptions.
Identify seasonal sales trends.
Analyze payment and shipping preferences.
Create an interactive business intelligence dashboard.
